  "result": "Perfect! All 159 tests pass. I've created a comprehensive date utility module:\n\n**New file `src/dates.js`:**\n\n1. **`isValidDate(text)`** \u2014 Validates date strings in 'YYYY-MM-DD' format:\n   - Checks format with regex\n   - Validates month (1-12) and day (1-31) ranges\n   - Confirms the date actually exists (rejects Feb 30, non-leap Feb 29, etc.)\n   - Returns boolean\n   - Works in UTC\n\n2. **`addDays(date, n)`** \u2014 Adds n days to a date string:\n   - Handles positive and negative days\n   - Crosses month and year boundaries correctly\n   - Returns date in 'YYYY-MM-DD' format\n   - Works in UTC\n\n3. **`daysBetween(a, b)`** \u2014 Calculates whole days between two dates:\n   - Returns b minus a (positive if b is later)\n   - Handles month/year boundaries\n   - Returns whole days (no fractional days)\n   - Works in UTC\n\n**Changes to `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Replaced local `validateIssueDate()` function with call to `isValidDate()`\n- Removed duplicate/redundant date validation logic\n- Now uses centralized date utilities\n\n**Tests added (22 new, 159 total):**\n- Valid date format and edge cases (leap years, year/month boundaries)\n- Invalid formats, months, days, non-existent dates\n- Adding positive/negative days with boundary crossing\n- Day calculations between dates (forward and backward)\n- Zero-day operations\n- Leap year handling (2024, 2000 are leap years; 2025, 1900 are not)\n- Integration test verifying createInvoice uses isValidDate\n\n**Key design:**\n- All dates are 'YYYY-MM-DD' strings throughout the system\n- All date arithmetic uses UTC, never local time zone\n- Centralized, reusable date functions\n\nAll 159 tests pass. \u2705",
